\end{figure}

\subsection{Collider-Relevant Mass Windows}

The HL-LHC is sensitive to KK resonances in the range
\begin{equation}
2.5~\text{TeV} \lesssim m_n \lesssim 8.5~\text{TeV}.
\end{equation}

For BP1--BP4, the first three KK modes lie within this window:
\begin{align}
m_1 &\in [2.78, 4.55]~\text{TeV}, \\
m_2 &\in [4.12, 6.48]~\text{TeV}, \\
m_3 &\in [5.45, 8.62]~\text{TeV}.
\end{align}

The non-equidistant spacing produces distinct resonance peaks in di-lepton,
di-photon, and di-jet channels.

