\subsection{Analytic vs Numerical Comparison}

We compare the analytic mass formula Eq.~(\ref{eq:full_mass}) with numerical
solutions of the Sturm--Liouville equation. The agreement is within 3\% for all
benchmark points.

\begin{figure}[h!]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.75\textwidth]{fig_analytic_vs_numerical.pdf}
\caption{Comparison between analytic (solid lines) and numerical (points)
KK masses for BP1--BP4. Agreement is within 3\%.}
\label{fig:analytic_vs_numerical}
\end{figure}

The anharmonic mass spectrum provides a clear experimental discriminator between
STME-RS-A and standard RS models.